 ;; ============================================================================
 ;; 1. Problem Statement & Empirical Root Causes
 ;; ============================================================================
 :bip/problem-statement
 {:root-causes
  [{:id "RC-CONTAG-1"
    :title "Live 6-validator Devnet still running N=3 Contagion sample parameters (E=2/2, R=2/1, D=2/2)"
    :detail "Even though `config/devnet-6-config` (`E=5/4, R=5/2, D=5/4, murmur-k=5`) was defined in `src/bitecho/config.cljc`, `mesh/build-initial-node-state` selected `config/devnet-config` (`E=2/2`) whenever `:network` was `:devnet`, and `scripts/cluster.sh` omitted Contagion sample parameters from the rendered `:protocol` block."}
   {:id "RC-CONTAG-2"
    :title "Unclamped Contagion thresholds stall delivery when active Basalt view is smaller than configured sample size"
    :detail "In `src/bitecho/state_machine.cljc`, `handle-receive-sieve-echo` and `handle-receive-contagion-ready` compared vote counts against raw `(:echo-threshold cfg)`, `(:ready-threshold cfg)`, and `(:delivery-threshold cfg)`. When `|active-sample| < threshold` (e.g. during cold boot, transient peer drop, or `mainnet-config` with `D-hat=17` on a cluster of `N <= 17`), Contagion delivery stalled permanently."}
   {:id "RC-CONTAG-3"
    :title "Unbounded `:contagion-known-ids` growth in `contagion/generate-summary` on every tick"
    :detail "In `src/bitecho/state_machine.cljc`, `:tick` passed the entire historical `:contagion-known-ids` set to `contagion/generate-summary`, causing anti-entropy summary payloads to grow linearly with node uptime."}
   {:id "RC-SOAK-1"
    :title "BUG-SOAK-01: Per-request `HttpClient` instantiation across 15 shell call sites leaks SelectorManager threads and ephemeral sockets"
    :detail "Creating a new `java.net.http.HttpClient` per request across `light_node.clj`, `http.clj`, `infra.clj`, `upnp.clj`, and `acme.clj` spawned a new `HttpClient-N-SelectorManager` thread and connection pool on every poll/submit/control call, exhausting ephemeral ports after ~30 minutes of continuous daemon soak."}
   {:id "RC-SOAK-2"
    :title "BUG-SOAK-02 & BUG-SOAK-03: Qualified `<domain>/<nickname>` directory lookup rejection and missing `artifact-put` relay auto-fallback / `K_vector` allowlist"
    :detail "`directory-lookup` and `directory-verify` rejected qualified names like `bitecho.org/vector` via `valid-petname?`; `handle-serve-line!` did not fall back to bootstrap relay URL when `conn-opts` omitted `:relay-url`; and `default-infra-policy` omitted `K_vector` from `doc-blog-signers`."}
   {:id "RC-SOAK-3"
    :title "DIAG-SOAK-03, B7 & P-LEG-1: 208 KB UDP `SO_RCVBUF` burst drops, redundant canonical snapshot disk writes, and unverified `:p2p-link-bind` wire handling"
    :detail "Default OS UDP receive buffers (212992 bytes) dropped bursts under 6-node + 4-agent traffic; `persistence/save-state-to-disk` re-encoded and rewrote unchanged snapshots on every save; and `light-core/handle-wire-payload` lacked a `:p2p-link-bind` handler to gate relay P2P leg opening on cryptographic signature verification."}]}

 ;; ============================================================================
 ;; 2. Architectural Pillars & Deliverables
 ;; ============================================================================
 :bip/pillars
 {:P-CONTAG-1
  {:title "Live 6-Validator Devnet on `devnet-6-config` (`E=5/4, R=5/2, D=5/4, murmur-k=5`) via Both Routes"
   :files ["src/bitecho/shell/mesh.clj"
           "scripts/cluster.sh"]
   :changes
   ["In `mesh/build-initial-node-state`: when `explicit-network` is `:devnet` and `(>= (max (count nodes-cfg) (count validators)) 6)`, automatically select `(config/devnet-6-config)` as `base-proto-cfg`."
    "In `mesh/rebind-restored-state`: when restoring a `:devnet` snapshot on a `>= 6`-validator cluster whose persisted config still has legacy `:echo-sample-size 2`, automatically upgrade the base Contagion sample parameters to `devnet-6-config` before merging explicit `:protocol` overrides."
    "In `scripts/cluster.sh`: render `:murmur-k 5 :echo-sample-size 5 :echo-threshold 4 :ready-sample-size 5 :ready-threshold 2 :delivery-sample-size 5 :delivery-threshold 4` in `:protocol`."]}

  :P-CONTAG-2
  {:title "Pure Adaptive Sample-Threshold Clamping (`effective-sample-threshold`)"
   :files ["src/bitecho/state_machine.cljc"]
   :changes
   ["Add pure public `(effective-sample-threshold configured-sample-size configured-threshold active-sample-count)` clamping thresholds proportionally to `max(1, min(|active-sample|, ceil((T_hat / S) * |active-sample|)))` when `1 <= |active-sample| < S`, while preserving exact `T_hat` when `|active-sample| >= S` or `|active-sample| = 0`."
    "Wire `effective-sample-threshold` into `handle-receive-sieve-echo` (`E-hat`) and `handle-receive-contagion-ready` (`R-hat` and `D-hat`)."]}

  :P-CONTAG-3
  {:title "Mainnet Small-N Contagion Stall Guard & Startup Diagnostic"
   :files ["src/bitecho/shell/mesh.clj"
           "src/bitecho/state_machine.cljc"]
   :changes
   ["Add pure `(mesh/validate-contagion-config proto-cfg validator-count)` emitting a structured `:contagion-threshold-clamped` diagnostic whenever raw `:delivery-threshold > N - 1`, while adaptive clamping ensures Contagion delivery remains reachable for any honest quorum."]}

  :P-CONTAG-4
  {:title "Bounded Trailing-Epoch Window for `contagion/generate-summary`"
   :files ["src/bitecho/config.cljc"
           "src/bitecho/contagion/core.cljc"
           "src/bitecho/state_machine.cljc"]
   :changes
   ["Add `:contagion-summary-window-epochs 16` to `config/default-config`."
    "Extend `contagion/generate-summary` with an optional 4th argument `max-ids-or-filter`."
    "In `state-machine/handle-tick`, filter `:contagion-known-ids` to message IDs within the trailing `:contagion-summary-window-epochs` using `:message-epochs` (falling back to all `:contagion-known-ids` when `:message-epochs` is empty)."]}

  :P-SOAK-1
  {:title "BUG-SOAK-01: Shared Process-Wide `HttpClient` Across All 15 Shell Call Sites"
   :files ["src/bitecho/shell/light_node.clj"
           "src/bitecho/shell/http.clj"
           "src/bitecho/shell/infra.clj"
           "src/bitecho/shell/upnp.clj"
           "src/bitecho/shell/acme.clj"]
   :changes
   ["Expose shared daemon-executor `default-http-client` and `default-http11-client` in `bitecho.shell.light-node` and `bitecho.shell.http` (plus shared `delay` clients in `upnp.clj` and `acme.clj`), replacing all 15 per-request `HttpClient/newBuilder` and `HttpClient/newHttpClient` sites while supporting optional `:http-client` in `opts` for test injection."]}

  :P-SOAK-2
  {:title "BUG-SOAK-02: Qualified `<domain>/<nickname>` Support in `directory-lookup`, `directory-verify`, and `directory-register`"
   :files ["src/bitecho/light_node/cli.cljc"
           "src/bitecho/light_node/core.cljc"
           "src/bitecho/shell/light_node.clj"]
   :changes
   ["Accept both `--nickname` and `--name` in `cli.cljc` and `core.cljc`, splitting qualified `<domain>/<nickname>` strings (e.g. `bitecho.org/vector`) into `:domain` and `:nickname` across `build-cmd-map`, `exec-directory-lookup`, `exec-directory-verify`, `exec-directory-register`, and `fetch-directory-descriptor!`."]}

  :P-SOAK-3
  {:title "BUG-SOAK-03 & P-SOAK-6: Auto-Relay Fallback on `artifact-put` / `serve` Signaling, Cross-Root-Subnet Wildcard Outer Gossip & `K_vector` Allowlist"
   :files ["src/bitecho/shell/light_node.clj"
           "src/bitecho/node_main.cljs"
           "src/bitecho/light_node/core.cljc"
           "src/bitecho/config.cljc"
           "src/bitecho/shell/infra.clj"]
   :changes
   ["In `handle-serve-line!` (`light_node.clj` and `node_main.cljs`), fall back `relay-url` to bootstrap relay URL (`infer-bootstrap-relay-url` / `https://ns1.bitecho.org` when bootstrap domain is `bitecho.org`) and mirror non-direct outbound envelopes from `handle-serve-line!` and `run-serve!` relay-poll responses to `relay-url`."
    "In `exec-offer` and `exec-accept` (`light_node/core.cljc`), use wildcard `\"*\"` outer gossip `:subnet-id` for burn-bearing root-subnet signaling envelopes, and recognize `\"bitecho.org\"` and `\"devnet.bitecho.org\"` as equivalent root subnets in `config/equivalent-subnet-id?`."
    "Add `k-vector-agent-pubkey` / `K_vector` (`302a300506032b6570032100365bd3dc35b4f609d6ac147c129c5b791798765b181d53341e58d6fcf1c6cd62`) and `default-dev-signers` to `bitecho.shell.infra/default-infra-policy`."]}

  :P-SOAK-4
  {:title "DIAG-SOAK-03: 4 MB (`4194304`) `SO_RCVBUF` on Light-Node & DNS UDP Sockets"
   :files ["src/bitecho/shell/light_node.clj"
           "src/bitecho/shell/dns.clj"]
   :changes
   ["Add `(configure-udp-receive-buffer! target rcvbuf-bytes)` in `bitecho.shell.light-node` setting `StandardSocketOptions/SO_RCVBUF` to 4 MB (`4194304`) on UDP `DatagramChannel`s and `DatagramSocket`s across `query-validator-chain-state!`, `dial-single-node!`, `dial-p2p-peer!`, `start-ingress-tcp-listener!`, and `dns/start-dns-server!`."]}

  :P-SOAK-5
  {:title "B7: Dirty-Gated Non-Canonical Local Snapshot Persistence"
   :files ["src/bitecho/shell/persistence.clj"]
   :changes
   ["Track last-saved stripped state and per-path metrics (`persistence-stats`: `:saved-count`, `:skipped-clean`) in `bitecho.shell.persistence/save-state-to-disk`, skipping redundant disk rewrites when stripped state is unchanged and encoding with non-canonical fast Fressian while `load-state-from-disk` decodes both canonical and standard Fressian."]}

  :P-LEG-1
  {:title "Verified `:p2p-link-bind` Wire Gate Before Opening Relay P2P Leg"
   :files ["src/bitecho/light_node/core.cljc"]
   :changes
   ["Add `handle-wire-p2p-link-bind` to `light-core/handle-wire-payload`: verify Ed25519 signature over `bitecho-p2p-link-bind-v1|<sender>|<session-id>` and verify `<sender>` matches the open session's `:peer` before transitioning the session P2P state to `:open` (`:connected? true :zero-burn? true`); reject invalid/forged link-binds with counted `[:diagnostics :p2p-link-bind-rejected]` and diagnostic event (Rule 5)."]}}

